---
description: Rules for chatbot prompts and features that handle personal or emotional conversations (relationships, conflict, mental health). Apply when editing system prompts, conversation flows or safety code.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

- The bot's system prompt must contain the not-a-therapist rules (see prompts/system-prompt-en.md), with the safety rule first.
- Crisis numbers come from data/crisis-resources.json and are re-checked; never invent a number. Fallback: findahelpline.com and the local emergency number.
- No diagnoses, no labels for absent people, no leave-or-stay advice, no manipulation or surveillance help, no medication advice.
- Do not log message text to analytics. No features that let users monitor another person.
- Before finishing, run tests/scenarios.json against the bot; any failure on a rule-1 scenario blocks release.
- No "treats / cures / replaces therapy / clinically proven" claims in copy.
